      "title": "System Uptime",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Continuous operating time since the switch was last reloaded or rebooted. Units: Seconds (formatted as Days, Hours, Minutes). Source: SNMPv2-MIB::sysUpTime (OID .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0). Limitations: Uptime resets during firmware upgrades, power cycles, or kernel crash reboots. Missing data indicates collector outage, agent failure, or network disruption; values are preserved as null gaps."
